DESCRIPTION:<b>REGISTRATION</b>: <a href="https://forms.office.com/Pages/R
 esponsePage.aspx?id=TsVyyzFKnk2xSh6jbfrJTI9QJhcY12JAolV5CeByrWpUQTUyMTk2V
 VVKRkZGUklITjEzTk1ZR0tWUC4u" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vi
 sit>Click Here</a>\n\n<i>NOTE: Registration closes 24 hours before event 
 start. Please register ahead of the event. Registrants will receive Zoom 
 information and related materials by email one week and within 24 hours b
 efore the event.</i>\n\nJoin an interactive event organized by ASIST. Res
 erve your seat at the Research Integrity Roundtable "Open Scholarship: Da
 ta Transparency\, Accessibility\, and Security" on Tuesday\, April 14th\,
  2026 at 5:30pm - 7:00pm EDT. This RCR-200 offering is designed for resea
 rchers at every stage of their career\, regardless of their discipline. P
 articipants will engage in an interactive virtual event to discuss the op
 en scholarship framework and how you can make your data accessible\, tran
 sparent\, and secure.\n\nThis event is only open to current Duke faculty\
 , staff\, and students. Attending this event fulfills the <b>RCR-200</b> 
 requirement for Faculty and Staff as well as the <b>714 RCR credit</b> fo
 r graduate students\, but participants must attend for 60 minutes and par
 ticipate in breakout room discussion to receive credit. \n\nContact: \nAS
 IST office \nASIST@duke.edu
DURATION:PT1H30M
